a quarterback for 5.1, a kicker for 1.0 and a wide receiver in the IDP slot for 2.6. That is 8.7 points from three roster spots. He lost by 8.68 and went 0-2. Do the math, it's already done."},{"winner":"1","loser":"5","winner_points":162.1,"loser_points":147.28,"margin":14.82,"note":"309 combined points, the best game on the board, and both managers should feel terrible. Andrew won it 162 to 147 with Caleb Williams and 37.26 points glued to his bench and Kyle Pitts posting a clean zero in his starting lineup. Tom had the single best roster in the league on Sunday, 179.18 points of it, and played 147.28. Mahomes and Goedert watched from the couch. That is the whole game, right there. The only mercy is that 147.28 cleared the median by 29.37, so Tom banked the half he did not have to think about and goes to 1-1."},{"winner":"7","loser":"3","winner_points":116.8,"loser_points":94.1,"margin":22.7,"note":"Nishil scored 116.80, which is 10 points below league average, and won by 23. That is what happens when the man across from you pays $63 for a receiver who catches two balls for 12 yards. Will's starting lineup featured $84 of wideout producing 4.6 points while a $1 rookie put up 12.9 on his bench. Zero all-play wins, and 0-2. But hold the parade in Gucci: 116.80 missed the median by 1.11, so winning by 22.70 bought Nishil a 1-1 anyway. One more catch anywhere on that roster and he is 2-0."},{"winner":"12","loser":"6","winner_points":155.6,"loser_points":125.58,"margin":30.02,"note":"Abhishek left 2.18 points on the bench, the best lineup management in the league that did not go clean, and it did not matter, because Darrius started Sam Darnold. Thirteen passing yards. 0.52 points. C.J. Stroud, also one dollar, also on the roster, threw for 274 and two scores from the bench. The $1 quarterback lottery has a losing ticket and Bend The Knee bought it. Darrius still cleared the median by 7.67, which is the fantasy equivalent of getting hit by a bus and keeping your wallet. 1-1."},{"winner":"10","loser":"13","winner_points":153.8,"loser_points":117.38,"margin":36.42,"note":"The preseason number one against the preseason number two, and it was over by the second quarter. Chris got 35.66 from Josh Allen and 33.1 from Gibbs and never looked back. Jon started a $22 tight end who did not play a snap, a quarterback who scored 6.44, and benched the guy who threw for 387. 110 points a week was the projection. This is the kind of week that makes a projection feel personal."},{"winner":"2","loser":"8","winner_points":157.06,"loser_points":104.48,"margin":52.58,"note":"The biggest beating of the week, 52.58, delivered by a man whose quarterback finished with 0.62 points. Barrett started Kyler Murray, watched him throw for 18 yards and an interception, and still put up 157.06 because Kenneth Walker went for 34.6 and Chuba Hubbard went for 22.2. Maclane got 24.96 from Lamar Jackson and then the rest of his roster filed for unemployment, 13 points under the median, 0-2."}],"top_starts":[{"slot":"RB","name":"Derrick Henry","pos":"RB","pts":35.8,"proj":14.02,"cost":45,"fa":false,"stats":"3 Rush TD, 144 Rush Yds, 19 Rec Yds","team":"The Asshouse Always Wins","team_id":"5","started":true,"vs_proj":21.78},{"slot":"QB","name":"Josh Allen","pos":"QB","pts":35.66,"proj":19.96,"cost":29,"fa":false,"stats":"334 Pass Yds, 2 Rush TD, 2 Pass TD","team":"Leo the Cleo","team_id":"10","started":true,"vs_proj":15.7},{"slot":"RB","name":"Kenneth Walker","pos":"RB","pts":34.6,"proj":13.28,"cost":43,"fa":false,"stats":"173 Rush Yds, 1 Rush TD, 1 Rec TD","team":"A dad","team_id":"2","started":true,"vs_proj":21.32},{"slot":"RB","name":"Jahmyr Gibbs","pos":"RB","pts":33.1,"proj":21.04,"cost":73,"fa":false,"stats":"156 Rush Yds, 2 Rush TD, 30 Rec Yds","team":"Leo the Cleo","team_id":"10","started":true,"vs_proj":12.06},{"slot":"RB","name":"D'Andre Swift","pos":"RB","pts":32.9,"proj":11.63,"cost":26,"fa":false,"stats":"3 Rush TD, 124 Rush Yds, 10 Rec Yds","team":"Hail Mary